{"abstract":"Blue denim, a billion-dollar industry, is currently dyed with indigo in an unsustainable process requiring harsh reducing and alkaline chemicals. Forming indigo directly in the yarn through indican (indoxyl-β-glucoside) is a promising alternative route with mild conditions. Indican eliminates the requirement for reducing agent while still ending as indigo, the only known molecule yielding the unique hue of blue denim. However, a bulk source of indican is missing. Here, we employ enzyme and process engineering guided by techno-economic analyses to develop an economically viable drop-in indican synthesis technology. Rational engineering of PtUGT1, a glycosyltransferase from the indigo plant, alleviated the severe substrate inactivation observed with the wildtype enzyme at the titers needed for bulk production. We further describe a mild, light-driven dyeing process. Finally, we conduct techno-economic, social sustainability, and comparative life-cycle assessments. These indicate that the presented technologies have the potential to significantly reduce environmental impacts from blue denim dyeing with only a modest cost increase.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bidart, Gonzalo Nahuel","Teze, David","Jansen, Charlotte Uldahl","Pasutto, Eleonora","Putkaradze, Natalia","Sesay, Anna Mamusu","Fredslund, Folmer","Lo Leggio, Leila","Ögmundarson, Olafur","Sukumara, Sumesh","Qvortrup, Katrine","Welner, Ditte Hededam"],"cuid":["S03-098.38-768467"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Qvortrup, Katrine","Welner, Ditte Hededam"],"country":["Iceland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Iceland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chemoenzymatic indican for light driven denim dyeing","src":["dtu","itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45749-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.38-768467","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10899603","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38413572","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85186235473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d78213e6-946e-4833-8da4-f92058de5022","itu-b77d23f7-f586-4239-9e14-7b953762f1b1","ku-c521cd54-bc84-4752-9c43-e087b3e57b84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DD003635BB0A6348DECAD793DC29932C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385221501/s41467_024_45749_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45749-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/354575581/s41467-024-45749-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Intera